# DeviceKey cloud-login freeze v53 (2026-11-03; IP-4 section 14.7 source review)
# Only two implementation digests change; all other 22 entries remain exact.
# Facade: the prior DA-4 internal ESP32 BLE four-slot branch requires both
# explicit selectors; no shared class members or public begin/login change.
# ESP32 WiFiBLE product: relative to the reviewed f878 graph, only the one-byte
# RAM startup intent, pre-attach request, once-only consume and explicit initial
# provisioning selection change. No NVS erase, grant or automatic rearm.
# DeviceKey proof/session wire, providers and MQTT algorithms remain unchanged.
# Selector include order is checked separately: only WiFiBLE loads maintained
# OfficialConfig before Facade; ordinary WiFi/BLE remain Facade-first.
# Previous v52 (2026-11-01; reviewed queued-RX renewal boundary)
# Only ManagedMqttTransport declarations/implementation change: gated consumers
# service the valid current MQTT connection before re-evaluating the local gate.
# Split, not increase, the transport operation budget; ordinary poll is unchanged.
# No member/callback retention, credential expiry extension or remote-ACK claim.
# Previous v51 (2026-11-01; reviewed existing QA-3 provisioned graph)
# Align only Facade, WiFiProduct, Esp32WiFiProv and Esp32WiFiBLEProduct:
# internal ESP32 SoftAP four-slot selection, no-extension hooks, actual native
# deinit observation, shared Client/carrier TaskSupport and guarded root/stop
# lifecycle. Includes the previously approved non-empty PoP option consumer.
# No new refresh logic, wire, public admission, slots, secrets or SDK changes.
# Previous v50 (2026-11-01; reviewed QA-3 bounded Task refresh deferral)
# Only HttpDeviceKeySessionProvider and ManagedMqttTransport declarations /
# implementations change: opt-in valid-old-credential deferral before provider
# poll, while MQTT continues. Normal poll, proof/session wire, expiry, auth
# failure and retries are unchanged. No additional members or credential copy.
# Previous v49 (2026-10-29; reviewed LOC-5 local input facade)
# Compared with c719d29, Facade adds only the location include, four location
# overloads and local loss/clear forwarding methods (21 added lines). No
# fields, begin arguments or DeviceKey/login/session/MQTT paths change.
# Local observation acceptance neither sends nor grants Cloud authorization.
# Only the Facade digest changes; every other frozen entry is preserved.
# Previous v48 (2026-10-17; R4 release/profile binding guard)
# Only the task build contract gains the required maintained-library binding.
# Existing SDK fault/heap entries, disabled graph, shared Facade and all other
# DeviceKey/login/session/MQTT implementation digests remain unchanged.
# Previous v46 (2026-10-16; reviewed R4 task candidate bounds)
# Only task-enabled R4 guards tighten to four-slot plain manual WiFi. The
# ordinary task-disabled graph, DeviceKey/login/session and MQTT stay unchanged.
# Previous v45 (2026-10-14; reviewed internal Wio task admission)
# Only the Facade platform guard adds the opt-in internal Wio task candidate.
# Shared class layout, defaults, APIs, login/session and MQTT remain unchanged.
# Previous v44 (2026-10-14; reviewed stable multi-TU facade)
# Product selection is a dependent entry helper, never conditional members or
# SelectedProfile binding in the shared BlinkerClass definition. The three
# public entry headers select only call-site packs; the global facade, 12 B
# ABI, begin arguments and existing TaskSupport/factory remain unchanged.
# Renesas Print is forward-declared as the Core's arduino::Print entity in
# every TU, preserving the existing native debug API independent of include order.
# Only the Facade digest changes; login/session/MQTT digests are preserved.
# Previous v43 (2026-10-14; reviewed internal R4 task seam)
# Facade admits only explicitly gated R4 manual-WiFi tasks. The R4 product
# selects the shared optional lifecycle/carrier only under that gate and an
# explicit capacity/policy; default remains the original WiFi composition.
# No facade fields, begin arguments, DeviceKey/login wire or MQTT changes.
# Only Facade and R4 product digests change in this revision.
# Previous v42 (2026-10-13; reviewed timeStatus observation)
# Facade adds only a read of the existing business clock snapshot, resetting
# output before the read. No fields, begin/login wire, credentials or time
# negotiation changes. Sketch Timer is separate and never enters this graph.
# All other frozen implementation digests remain unchanged.
# Previous v41 (2026-09-24; reviewed typed task facade opt-in)
# TaskSupport adds an explicit property allowlist before begin; no facade
# instance fields, login credentials, begin signature or MQTT changes.
# WiFi lifecycle selects one optional carrier and task lifecycle wrapper;
# default extension keeps the original carrier/lifecycle, no extra state.
# Shared business clock and read-only DeviceKey source are borrowed. Login
# provider, key/proof/session wire, MQTT engine and public begin are unchanged.
# Host 70-target regression and disabled/enabled firmware gates cover the seam;
# task authority retirement/hardware admission remain explicit pending work.
# Previous v39 (2026-09-13; reviewed B3-4c own time)
# WiFiBLE versus B3-4b installed source: only attachTime using existing stack
# tick/RNG/Client. No new members, login/provisioning wire or begin changes.
# Previous v38 (2026-09-13; reviewed B3-3 optional time)
# Review: Facade opt-in enableTime/time API and WiFiProduct attachTime injection.
# Borrowed business-time service only; default off, begin arguments, DeviceKey,
# login proof/session wire, TLS/security clocks and all other hashes unchanged.
# Previous v37: reviewed B2b-12 recovery.
# B1 review: HTTP transport truncation retries the same request, completed
# malformed CBOR/authentication still fails closed; expose Backoff and dropped
# MQTT socket errors. B2b-12/13 host 58/58 plus real login/reboot/revocation.
# Login wire, golden vectors, proof/key material and public begin unchanged.
# Previous v36 (2026-09-12; D1b optional diagnostic output):
# Facade review: only an IDiagnosticOutput debug overload and API comments.
# begin/login/provisioning implementation and all other hashes unchanged.
# v35 changed only WiFiProduct's stopped-state candidate Retry policy injection.
# Login wire/authentication and transactional provisioning defaults are unchanged.
# Session contract/provider/Key/ManagedMQTT/golden hashes are unchanged.
# Cloud is attached first so it polls revocation before LAN output. Default
# NoWifiProductExtension adds no sockets, credentials, queue or SDK dependency.
# Preserve the successful 16 B login proof separately from HTTP scratch.
# Optional shared cloud wrapper handles local-control without a second MQTT.
# Default products allocate no control table/queue; public begin and login wire
# remain unchanged. AuthenticationRequired remains fail-closed.
# Hashes cover non-empty implementation text but omit #include paths and blank
# layout lines. Dependency/layout changes have separate architecture/package
# gates. Implementation changes still require review and an explicit update.
